      "text_raw": "Active entities: Ariel Pink, Chillwave, Daniel Lopatin, Wolfgang Voigt, Hypnagogic pop, Matrix Metals, witch house, YouTube. Topic: History and legacy Precursors Vaporwave artwork Pitchfork reviewed the album Life [ 42][nb 3 ] Washed Out 's \" Feel It All Around \" ( June 2009 ) , which slowed down the 1983 Italian dance song \" I Want You \" by Gary Low , exemplified the \" analog nostalgia \" of chillwave that vaporwave artists sought to reconfigure[4 ] Vaporwave was subsumed under a larger \" Tumblr esthetic \" \" A1 \" from Eccojams Vol . 1 ( 2010 ) that had become fashionable in underground digital music 0:31 and art scenes of the 2010s.[59 ] In 2010 , Lopatin included A track from Daniel Lopatin 's Eccojams , an album which pitch- shifts and distorts 1980s pop music . The sample in this excerpt is \" Africa \" by Toto . [ 58 ] several of the tracks from Memory Vague , as well as a few new ones , on his album Chuck Person 's Eccojams Vol . 1 , released in August under the alias \" Chuck Person\".[60 ] With packaging that resembled the 1993 video game Ecco the Problems playing this file ? See media help . Dolphin , the album inspired a host of suburban teens and young adults to formulate what would become vaporwave.[3 ] Seapunk followed in mid-2011 as an aquatic-themed Tumblr subculture and Internet meme[61 ] that presaged vaporwave in its concern for \" spacey \" electronic music and GeoCities web graphics.[12 ] Upcoming entities: Ferraro, Lopatin, Miles Bowe, Robin Burnett, Far Side Virtual, Last FM, Luxury Elite, MediaFire. Next focus: it was defined engagement",
