      "text_raw": "Active entities: James Culpepper, Jared Hartmann, Lacey Nicole Mosley, Lacey Nicole Sturm, Lacey Sturm, née Mosley, Pat Seals, Sameer Bhattacharya. Topic: Sturm became the first solo female artist Discovered a Life Worth Living , Sturm explained that a primary reason for her leaving the band was the death of the band 's Occupations Singer · songwriter · author sound engineer . The band performed one last show as a Years active 2000–present means to help the sound engineer 's wife and child . This Member of Flyleaf experience caused Sturm to consider her own son and wonder Spouse Joshua Sturm ​ ( m. 2008 ) ​ what she would do if she knew she had only one more year Website laceysturm.com with him . \" It was really amazing to recognize this season changing in my life and the freedom that I was gon na be able to focus on my family \" , Sturm said . \" And although it was really hard , I 'm thankful . And that 's the reason I stepped down from Flyleaf . \"[8][9 ] On November 7 , 2022 , it was announced by Flyleaf that Sturm had returned to the band , with the band now calling themselves \" Flyleaf with Lacey Sturm\"[10 ] Guest appearances ​ [ edit ] Sturm provided backing vocals on \" Run to You \" and \" Born Again \" , two tracks on Christian rock band Third Day 's 2008 album Revelation.[11 ] She received a Grammy nomination at the 52nd Sturm in 2008 Best Gospel Performance.[12 ] Grammy Awards for her feature on \" Born Again \" by Third Day for She has also worked with Apocalyptica on their song \" Broken Pieces \" and with Orianthi on the song \" Courage\"[13 ] She recorded a song , \" Heavy Prey \" , for the Underworld : Awakening soundtrack[14 ] She was a guest vocalist on the 2013 track \" Take the Bullets Away \" by We as Human[15 ] Upcoming entities: Ben Hull, Josh Sturm, Lacey, Sturm, Tom Gascon, the Billboard Hard Rock Albums, Top Rock Albums.[3, Greensboro. Next focus: she performed as a guest vocalist in Breaking Benjamin",
